{
  "id": "ep075",
  "duration": 54.173,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.018,
      "text": "The Moon's brightest rocks are too young to exist.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Back side of the Moon AS16-3021.jpg",
        "credit": "Apollo 16 astronauts",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Back_side_of_the_Moon_AS16-3021.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.033,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.018,
      "end": 11.138,
      "text": "In 1972, Apollo 16 astronauts returned stunningly bright stones called anorthosite from the lunar highlands.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "John W. Young on the Moon.jpg",
        "credit": "Charlie Duke",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_W._Young_on_the_Moon.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.033,
          "end": 7.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.067,
          "end": 11.133,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.138,
      "end": 17.608,
      "text": "For decades, experts believed these rocks floated like icebergs atop a primordial magma ocean.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA-Apollo8-Dec24-Earthrise.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Bill Anders",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA-Apollo8-Dec24-Earthrise.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.133,
          "end": 13.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 13.867,
          "end": 17.6,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.608,
      "end": 24.928,
      "text": "This coarse-grained crust is 90 percent plagioclase feldspar, a mineral that is less dense than liquid magma.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Lunar anorthosite descartes highlands (36131355931).jpg",
        "credit": "the paleobear from Lontananza, Loreto, Peru",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lunar_anorthosite_descartes_highlands_(36131355931).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.6,
          "end": 24.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.928,
      "end": 35.673,
      "text": "But in 2011, researchers used precise chemical dating on lunar Sample 60025 and found it was only 4.36 billion years old.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.933,
          "end": 35.667,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.673,
      "end": 41.498,
      "text": "This age is over 100 million years too young for a crust formed at the Moon's birth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.667,
          "end": 41.5,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.498,
      "end": 48.543,
      "text": "This discovery suggests the Moon was volcanically active much later than scientists ever imagined.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA18821-LunarGrailMission-OceanusProcellarum-Rifts-Closeup-20141001.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Colorado School of Mines/MIT/JPL/GSFC",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA18821-LunarGrailMission-OceanusProcellarum-Rifts-Closeup-20141001.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.5,
          "end": 48.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 48.543,
      "end": 53.823,
      "text": "Geologists are now forced to rewrite the entire ancient history of our closest neighbor.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Back side of the Moon AS16-3021.jpg",
        "credit": "Apollo 16 astronauts",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Back_side_of_the_Moon_AS16-3021.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 48.533,
          "end": 54.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
